{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789490182,"nonce":"4BtGdpTCCBrQVrhuGbtYZYl6F7s=","title":"Spike standalone file workers","message":"## Parent\n\ngit-bug issue `60b2077` — PRD: GIC v0.9 workshop environment\n\n## What to build\n\nEstablish whether one self-contained HTML artifact opened directly through `file://` can create, cancel, replace, and time out Blob workers in Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit. Recommend the smallest single-file isolation strategy supported by evidence.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] One generated artifact opens directly from disk without a server or network request in all three browser engines.\n- [ ] Editing the artifact schedules a replacement run after 100 ms and prevents stale worker results from updating the page.\n- [ ] A long-running program is terminated and produces a visible timeout failure without freezing the page.\n- [ ] Canvas, diagnostics, runtime failures, and structured output cross the worker boundary as plain data.\n- [ ] Any engine-specific failure is reproduced and documented with exact browser versions.\n- [ ] The resulting decision selects Blob workers or another single-file isolation method before production export work.\n\n## Blocked by\n\nNone - can start immediately.","files":null}]}